    "updated_at": "2015-12-27T01:08:03Z",
    "body": "https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/HTMLCanvasElement/toDataURL  \n\nHere it says that there's an optional second argument that controls the image quality, _if_ the image type is `image/jpeg` or `image/webp`, otherwise it's ignored.  \nI just tested on Chrome 47 and Firefox 42, and it's true, the length of the resulting data URI changes.\nnode-canvas taking a callback as second argument would definitely be an incompatibility.\n",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
