    "updated_at": "2015-12-27T20:18:52Z",
    "body": "Yeah, this seems pretty bad. I think we should spec that the second argument is a number between 0 and 1, and explain what the expected behavior is if anything else is passed (e.g. a negative number, a number greater than 1, a function, ...). Users agents \"may\" use that number to indicate quality, etc. etc.\n",
