    "updated_at": "2016-01-04T14:05:15Z",
    "body": "I suppose we could start throwing in some cases, like if you pass in a function, but NaN shouldn't throw since it seems reasonable to expect code to pass in `undefined` and divide it by 100. NaN should probably be equivalent to omitting the argument. But I haven't checked what implementations do.\n",
