    "created_at": "2016-01-04T15:09:58Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-01-04T15:09:58Z",
    "body": "Currently an implementation could be conformant with literally any interpretation of the second onward arguments. For example interpreting the second argument as a callback, or as a quality number between 0 and MAX_INT, or as the title to set for the window while decoding. Or interpreting all arguments after the first as additional types to decode to, concatenating the results. This seems bad. We should spec what browsers implement (a single quality argument between 0 and 1, with further arguments ignored).\n",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
